+/* INSTALLER-WINDOW-GROW (A5): Installer 43.3 opens a window of Height 17 * YSize + 23 (YSize = the screen font's height, clamped
+ * 8..100; routine 0x2b4, s66 a5-installer.md) and lays its two button rows out from the bottom with a 1 px margin. The patch
+ * recognises the program by name (win_is_installer_name: the task or CLI command name's last path part is "Installer",
+ * any case) and by that formula (win_installer_grow: the requested height is exactly the stock one, so an Installer with
+ * another sizing, e.g. 47.x, or any other window of that name is left alone). The window gets YSize / 2 more rows (5 at
+ * helvetica 11: a 6 px bottom margin), its top moves up half of that (it stays centred), never above the screen's title
+ * bar, and its bottom never below the usable bottom (the screen's height minus the bar strip): the growth shrinks to what
+ * fits. 1 when b changed. */
+int win_is_installer_name(const char *name);
+int win_installer_grow(win_box *b, int ysize, const win_screen *s);
+
 /* win:snap: the box of one zone of the work area. WA_LEFT / WA_RIGHT / WA_UP / WA_DOWN halves, WA_TL / WA_TR / WA_BL /
  * WA_BR quarters (cells split at (size - gap) / 2, the remainder pixel to the right / bottom cell), WA_CENTER keeps the
  * window's size and centres it. Every size goes through win_fit. 1 when the box changed, 0 when not or arg is no zone. */
